# Owner workflow preferences

## Requests

- Plain-English user stories work best (“when X is cancelled, notify Y if Z”)
- Attach screenshots for UI bugs — describe what you see vs what you expect
- One focused change per message when possible; short follow-ups are fine (“remove from month grid”)

## Git

- **Commit** only when explicitly asked
- **Push** when the user says push / deploy / “push changes”
- Do not force-push `main`

## After implementing

- Say what changed in plain language, not just file names
- Mention if user should refresh admin or save Settings once to normalize data
- Run relevant tests (`test:messages`, `test:waitlist`) and `tsc` for non-trivial changes

## When stuck on UI

- Prefer fixing root cause over patches (e.g. contenteditable over misaligned overlays)
- Ask one clarifying question only if behaviour is genuinely ambiguous
